_river_and_tributaries.png/500px-Lower_Aber_river_and_tributaries.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lower_Aber_river_and_tributaries.png/500px-Lower_Aber_river_and_tributaries.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The source of the Blue Nile is Gish Abay at the bottom of the bright line. The river flows north from there to Lake Tana at the top.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALower_Aber_river_and_tributaries.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Hippos_in_their_Natural_Habitat_in_Kazinga_Channel_10.jpg/500px-Hippos_in_their_Natural_Habitat_in_Kazinga_Channel_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Hippos_in_their_Natural_Habitat_in_Kazinga_Channel_10.jpg/500px-Hippos_in_their_Natural_Habitat_in_Kazinga_Channel_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHippos_in_their_Natural_Habitat_in_Kazinga_Channel_10.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Nymphaea_lotus1XMATT.jpg/500px-Nymphaea_lotus1XMATT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Nymphaea_lotus1XMATT.jpg/500px-Nymphaea_lotus1XMATT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The white Egyptian lotus is native to still waters of the Nile Basin.[91]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANymphaea_lotus1XMATT.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Murchison_Falls%2C_Uganda_%2823475021234%29.jpg/500px-Murchison_Falls%2C_Uganda_%2823475021234%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai